UPDATE companies SET description='BEI Precision traces its roots to 1862 when D.H. Baldwin founded the D.H. Baldwin Company in Cincinnati, Ohio, initially building pianos and later electronic organs. The optical encoder technology emerged from the development of "Tone Wheels" for organs, and the company now operates from Maumelle, Arkansas, where its manufacturing plant continues that legacy of precision.

The company designs and manufactures high‑precision optical encoders — housed and un‑housed (kit) designs, absolute and incremental, single‑turn and multi‑turn — as well as flight‑worthy pivot‑and‑jewel accelerometers, displacement sensors, and rotary optical scanners. All products are designed and manufactured in the USA, available in both ITAR‑controlled and EAR‑regulated configurations, and supported by a broad engineering network and robust supply chain for custom and sole‑source solutions.

BEI serves defense primes, aerospace OEMs, and government programs across air, land, sea, and space domains. Its encoders provide gimbal feedback for airborne ISR payloads, precision angular measurement for weapons targeting systems, and closed‑loop positioning in next‑generation combat vehicles. Accelerometers are deployed in fixed‑wing, rotary‑wing, and unmanned platforms for flight control and vibration monitoring, while optical scanners support EO/IR systems in ISR payloads, weapons sighting, and airborne surveillance.

A long heritage of sole‑source programs with defense primes and ITAR‑compliant domestic production underpin its position in mission‑critical sensing.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Optical encoder design and manufacturing (housed, un\u2011housed, absolute, incremental, single\u2011turn, multi\u2011turn)", "Accelerometer manufacturing (pivot\u2011and\u2011jewel, displacement sensors)", "Optical scanner manufacturing (rotary)", "Custom and sole\u2011source engineering", "Mil\u2011spec ruggedization", "ITAR\u2011compliant manufacturing", "EAR\u2011regulated configurations"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Space", "Military", "Government", "Scientific", "Commercial space"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ITAR\u2011compliant manufacturing in the USA", "Sole\u2011source heritage with defense primes", "Custom engineering to exact interface, envelope, and performance specs", "Mil\u2011spec ruggedization for extreme environments", "Over 60 years of optical encoder technology advancement"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1862 as D.H. Baldwin Company in Cincinnati, Ohio -> /about", "Headquarters in Maumelle, Arkansas -> db, /, /about", "Products: optical encoders, accelerometers, optical scanners -> /", "ITAR\u2011compliant and EAR\u2011regulated manufacturing -> /, certifications", "Markets: air, land, sea, space -> /", "Customers: defense primes, aerospace OEMs, government programs -> /", "Applications: gimbal feedback, weapons targeting, combat vehicles, flight control, vibration monitoring, EO/IR systems -> /", "Sole\u2011source heritage with defense primes -> /", "Mil\u2011spec ruggedization for extreme environments -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All BEI optical encoders are designed and manufactured in the USA", "founded_year": "1862", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "EAR\u2011regulated"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/beiprecision/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bei-precision' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BMES operates its national repair center in Louisville, Kentucky, minutes from the UPS Worldport hub.

The company provides depot repair services for patient monitors, telemetry transmitters, infusion pumps, bedside modules, O2 blenders, suction regulators, and fetal transducers. Every device undergoes a 7-Step Critical Care Process that includes decontamination, component-level board repair, OEM-spec calibration, and quality-control verification. BMES also sells refurbished equipment and medical accessories such as cables, leads, and test equipment. The Louisville facility serves a nationwide customer base and reports a 95% first-pass repair success rate at flat-rate pricing.

Customers include hospital biomedical departments and healthcare systems such as UK HealthCare, University of Louisville Health, Tampa General Hospital, and Mt. Carmel New Albany Surgical Hospital.

BMES was started to reduce equipment downtime with quality repairs, summarized in its purpose "Keeping Equipment Healthy for Patient Care." Differentiators cited by the company include a dedicated account representative for each facility, free shipping labels with UPS pickup, a 3-5 business day turnaround on core repairs, and a six-month Confident Care Warranty that covers the entire device rather than just the repaired component.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Depot repair of patient monitors", "Depot repair of telemetry transmitters", "Depot repair of infusion pumps", "Depot repair of bedside modules", "Depot repair of O2 blenders", "Depot repair of suction regulators", "Depot repair of fetal transducers", "7-Step Critical Care Process", "Decontamination and isolation protocol", "Component-level board repair", "Software troubleshooting and repair", "OEM-specification calibration", "Quality control verification and cosmetic testing", "Protective packaging and expedited return shipping", "Refurbished equipment sales", "Medical accessory and parts sales (cables, leads, test equipment)"], "industries": ["Healthcare facilities", "Hospital biomedical engineering departments", "Biomedical equipment repair", "Medical equipment repair"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "3-5 business days for core repairs", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Flat-rate pricing on all depot repairs", "3-5 business day turnaround for core repairs", "Six-month Confident Care Warranty covering the whole device", "Dedicated account representative per facility", "Free UPS shipping labels with pickup service", "95% first-pass repair success rate at flat rate"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 -> db", "Headquarters in Louisville, Kentucky -> db", "Specializes in patient monitor and telemetry repair -> /", "Depot repair services with flat-rate pricing, 3-5 day turnaround, 6-month warranty -> /", "7-Step Critical Care Process -> /about-us", "95% first-pass repair success rate at flat rate -> /about-us", "Nationwide customer base, facility near UPS Worldport -> /about-us", "Refurbished equipment sales and medical accessories -> /", "Case study with UK HealthCare saving 1,190 hours -> /", "Customer testimonials from University of Louisville Health, Tampa General Hospital, Mt. Carmel New Albany Surgical Hospital -> /", "Dedicated account representative per facility -> /", "Free UPS shipping labels with pickup -> /", "Confident Care Warranty covers whole device for six months -> /about-us", "Purpose: Keeping Equipment Healthy for Patient Care -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "BMES has specialized in patient monitor and telemetry repair since 1989. Our depot repair services keep your equipment in top shape with flat-rate pricing, 3-5 day turnaround, and a 6-month warranty on every repair.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/bmes---biomedical-equipment-service-company/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bmes' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BOH Electronics, a custom cable and wire harness manufacturer, is headquartered in River Falls, Wisconsin. After rapid growth, the operation moved to a 6,000-square-foot facility in 2006 and then to a 17,000-square-foot historic building in North Hudson in 2009, which underwent a certified historic rehabilitation completed in 2010. In July 2023, BOH relocated to a modern facility in the Whitetail Ridge Corporate Park in River Falls to support continued expansion.

The company produces custom cables, wire harness assemblies, and wire processing solutions, offering services that include design assistance, prototyping, electrical manufacturing, and electronic quality testing and inspection. Its product lines cover electronic wire harnesses, cable assemblies, wire processing, electromechanical assemblies, and overmolded and imported cables. BOH operates with no minimum volume requirements, handling orders ranging from a few pieces to thousands per week, and emphasizes quick turnaround and just-in-time delivery.

BOH serves original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), contract manufacturers, and a broad range of technology industries. Its customer base includes companies needing custom interconnect solutions for electronic and electromechanical applications.

The company highlights its factory-direct shipping, ISO 9001:2008 certification, RoHS compliance, and UL registration as key differentiators, along with a commitment to exceeding expectations through competitive pricing, 100% quality guarantee, and incomparable client relations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','RoHS','UL Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design Assistance and Prototyping", "Electrical Manufacturing and Production", "Electronic Quality Testing & Inspection", "Custom Packaging", "Just-in-Time Delivery", "Quick Turnaround", "IPC Standards Compliance", "UL Registered", "Expert Technical Support", "Wire Harness Assembly", "Cable Assembly", "Wire Processing", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Overmolded Cable Assembly"], "industries": ["OEM", "Contract Manufacturing", "Technology Industries"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high volume; no minimum order (1 to thousands per week)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order quantities (1 to thousands per week)", "Quick turnaround and just-in-time delivery", "Factory-direct shipping", "ISO 9001:2008 certified and RoHS compliant", "Custom prototyping and design assistance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 by Ben Hanke in Hudson, WI -> /about", "Relocated to River Falls, WI in July 2023 -> /", "ISO 9001:2008 certified in 2010 -> /about", "RoHS compliant -> /about, db", "No volume minimums, 1 to thousands per week -> /", "Custom cables, wire harness assemblies, wire processing -> /", "Industries: OEM, Contract Manufacturing, technology industries -> /", "Facility: 17,000 sq ft historic building in North Hudson (2009-2023) -> /about", "Current facility in Whitetail Ridge Corporate Park, River Falls -> /", "Services: Design Assistance, Prototyping, Electrical Manufacturing, Quality Testing & Inspection -> /", "Products: Wire Harnesses, Cable Assemblies, Wire Processing, Electromechanical Assemblies, Overmolded & Imported Cables -> /", "UL Registered -> /", "Quick Turn-around, Just in Time Delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "BOH Electronics is a premier cable and wire harness manufacturer.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order (1 piece)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='boh-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BAFS Inc. operates from Bangor, Maine, where it has spent over two decades serving the airline catering industry and related food-service sectors. The company does not disclose a founding year or founder names, and its ownership structure is not publicly stated.

The facility produces frozen entrée components, center-of-plate items, bulk sauces, starches, and medical or therapeutic meals for special dietary needs. Services include frozen food manufacturing, co-packaging, custom formulation, and private-label production, with product development offered from concept through production. The company emphasizes lower production minimums but does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

Customers span commercial airlines and inflight kitchens, cruise lines, rail-car dining operators, senior-nutrition programs such as Meals on Wheels, healthcare meal providers, and the U.S. Department of Defense. The company also supplies medical and therapeutic entrees for specialized diets.

BAFS highlights its registered dietitian who reviews every product to exceed nutritional standards, and it promotes a full product-development cycle from initial concept to finished goods as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','FDA inspected','USDA inspected','Department of Defense inspected','Third-party audited']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Frozen food manufacturing", "Frozen food co-packaging", "Custom food manufacturing", "Private label manufacturing", "Product development (concept to production)", "Co-packing"], "industries": ["Airline inflight catering", "Cruise line dining", "Rail car dining", "Senior nutrition", "Healthcare meals", "Meals on Wheels", "Department of Defense", "Medical and therapeutic meals"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Registered dietitian oversight on all products", "Lower production minimums", "Full product development from concept to production", "Multiple federal and third-party inspections (HACCP, FDA/USDA, DoD)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bangor, Maine -> db", "Over twenty years experience in airline catering -> db", "HACCP certification -> db", "FDA & USDA inspected -> /", "Department of Defense inspected -> /", "Third party audited -> /", "Frozen food manufacturing -> /", "Frozen food co-packaging -> /", "Custom food manufacturing -> /", "Private label manufacturing -> /", "Product development from concept to production -> db", "Lower production minimums -> db", "Entr\u00e9e components, center-of-plate components, bulk sauces and starches -> db", "Medical and therapeutic entrees and components -> db", "Industries: airline inflight catering, cruise line dining, rail car dining -> db, /", "Senior nutrition, healthcare meals, Meals on Wheels -> /", "Department of Defense as customer -> db, /", "Registered dietitian ensures products exceed standard -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New En