UPDATE companies SET description='Ballard Marine Fabricators operates from Seattle, Washington, where it was founded in 1986. The shop is 100% welder-owned by three partners—Matt DeVore, Chris Hanson, and Jim Clack—who together bring over 40 years of combined experience in steel vessel repair, aluminum boat building, boiler making, and exhaust systems. The trio launched the business after the fabrication shop they worked for closed without notice, prompting them to start their own operation the very next day.

The company functions as a custom fabrication job shop, producing marine exhaust systems, fuel tanks, handrails, hull repairs, radar and solar arches, offshore brackets, and residential metalwork such as stairs, cable railings, and countertops.

Concrete projects include code-compliant hull repairs that return vessels to service, exhaust systems built to outlast competitors, and elegant radar arches that integrate power mounting for electronics.

The founders emphasize merging their passion for welding and creative problem-solving to deliver solutions that not only look great but stand the test of time.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding (steel, aluminum)", "Exhaust system fabrication", "Fuel tank fabrication", "Handrail fabrication", "Hull repair", "Radar arch fabrication", "Solar arch fabrication", "Residential metal fabrication (stairs, cable railings, countertops)", "Offshore bracket fabrication", "Steel vessel repair", "Aluminum boat building", "Boiler making"], "industries": ["Marine", "Boat building", "Vessel repair", "Offshore", "Residential construction"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom exhaust systems built to outlast competitors", "Fuel tanks fabricated to custom specifications for long service life", "Hull repairs performed to code for safe return to service", "Radar and solar arches designed as elegant power mounting solutions", "Residential metalwork including stairs, cable railings, and countertops"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Seattle, Washington -> db", "Three founders: Matt DeVore, Chris Hanson, Jim Clack -> / (Meet the Team)", "100% welder-owned -> / (Meet the Team)", "Over 40 years combined experience -> / (Meet the Team)", "Started after previous employer closed fabrication shop -> / (Meet the Team)", "Specializes in custom exhaust systems -> / (Home: About)", "Offers fuel tanks, handrails, hull repair, radar/solar arches, residential metalwork, offshore brackets -> / (Home: About)", "Capabilities include steel vessel repair, aluminum boat building, boiler making -> / (Meet the Team)", "Facility at 1521 NW Ballard Way, Seattle -> / (Contact)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in high-quality custom exhaust systems, we are extremely capable in a wide range of different projects.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "3", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ballard-marine-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bare Wood Furniture Center opened in 2007 in Carencro, Louisiana, as a family-owned retailer of solid wood furniture. Founders Dennis and Natalie built the business to serve the greater Acadiana area, later joined by their daughter and son to meet growing demand. The showroom sits off I-49 at Exit 7 between Carencro and Sunset.

Unlike many furniture stores, Bare Wood allows customers to take purchased pieces home the same day, eliminating wait times for special orders. The inventory spans a range of styles and sizes, all priced to remain affordable year-round.

The retailer serves residential customers across the Acadiana region, focusing on households seeking durable, heirloom-quality furnishings. Its customer base includes repeat buyers who return for additional pieces and referrals, reflecting the company''s emphasis on long-term relationships.

The business was founded on the belief that high-quality solid wood furniture should be accessible and lasting. The family highlights its commitment to customer satisfaction through a guarantee that extends beyond the sale, offering support for repairs or issues after delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail and showroom sales", "Immediate inventory availability (same-day take-home)", "Product curation and supplier selection", "Post-sale customer support and repair assistance", "Customer relationship management"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Solid wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day for in-stock showroom pieces", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day take-home availability for in-stock showroom pieces", "Family-owned and operated since 2007", "Customer satisfaction guarantee with post-sale repair support", "Curated selection from multiple quality suppliers", "Affordable pricing maintained year-round"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 -> db", "Headquarters Carencro, Louisiana -> db", "Family-owned, founders Dennis and Natalie -> /", "Showroom location off I-49 at Exit 7 between Carencro and Sunset -> /", "Same-day take-home for showroom pieces -> /", "Customer satisfaction guarantee with post-sale support -> /", "Curated selection from multiple suppliers -> /", "Serves greater Acadiana area -> /", "Affordable pricing all year -> /", "Emphasis on building lasting relationships -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We keep our showroom stocked with unique, quality, real wood pieces that come from an ever expanding list of companies.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bare-wood-furniture-center' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barney & Carey Lumber Specialties operates from Avon, Massachusetts, but traces its roots to 1922 when the Barney & Carey Company Inc. was founded on the banks of the Neponset River in nearby Milton.

The company runs a specialty lumberyard stocking rare and exotic hardwoods alongside a custom millwork shop equipped with CNC machining centers. Its capabilities include precision CNC woodworking for custom cabinet parts, prototypes, and period millwork; custom molding production supported by over 350 knife profiles that can be cut in any species; and furniture refinishing and restoration for heirloom pieces. The shop serves both trade professionals and individual woodworkers, offering milling, cutting, and planing services on any material in inventory.

Customers range from contractors and trade professionals on commercial and historic restoration projects to hobbyists and homeowners. Notable projects cited by the company include the 4,000-bottle wine cellar for Boston’s XV Beacon hotel, a 25-foot period dining table for a Newport mansion owner, the reception area of a Manhattan skyscraper, and a Madison Avenue storefront. An online cabinet design tool allows customers to specify and order custom parts without a sales consultation.

The company emphasizes quality and service as its foundation, highlighting that its custom moldings are produced without the “skip” or “chatter” common in mass-produced profiles, and that pricing is often comparable to stock patterns. The availability of reclaimed species such as American Elm and a broad selection of exotic woods further differentiate its material offering.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Specialty lumber sales", "Custom millwork", "CNC woodworking", "CNC machining", "Furniture refinishing", "Custom cabinet parts", "Custom moldings", "Trim reproduction", "Period millwork", "Online cabinet design tool", "Milling", "Cutting", "Planing"], "industries": ["Construction trades", "Historic restoration", "Hospitality", "Commercial construction", "High-end residential", "DIY woodworking"], "materials": ["Specialty hardwoods", "Exotic woods", "Reclaimed American Elm", "American Ash", "Beech", "Eastern White Pine", "Radiata Pine", "C-select pine", "Lauan"], "equipment": ["CNC machines", "Milling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 350 knife profiles for custom moldings in any species", "Custom moldings free of skip or chatter", "Online self-service cabinet design and ordering", "Reclaimed and rare wood inventory (e.g., reclaimed American Elm)", "Full-service lumberyard with CNC milling for contractors and hobbyists"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1922 on banks of Neponset River in Milton, MA -> db", "Headquarters in Avon, MA -> /", "Specialty lumberyard with rare/exotic woods -> /", "CNC machining capabilities -> /", "Custom millwork with over 350 knife profiles -> /about", "Furniture refinishing services -> /", "Serves contractors and hobbyists -> /", "Projects: XV Beacon hotel, Newport mansion, Manhattan skyscraper, Madison Ave storefront -> /about", "Online cabinet design tool -> /", "Reclaimed Elm lumber -> /about", "No skip or chatter on custom moldings -> /about", "Materials: American Ash, Beech, Eastern White Pine, Radiata Pine, C-select pine, Lauan -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "With our milling equipment and CNC, we can mill, cut, and plane anything you need from any material we have available.", "founded_year": "1922", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='barney-and-carey-lumber-specialties' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barnhardt Manufacturing Co. was founded in 1900 in Charlotte, North Carolina, and has operated continuously for over 125 years. The company began as a cotton purification business and has since expanded into a family of brands that includes Carolina Absorbent Cotton and NCFI.

Today, Barnhardt produces purified cotton in traditional, organic, and reclaimed forms, supplying cotton, polyester, and rayon coils to the pharmaceutical and vitamin industries.

The company serves customers in pharmaceuticals, vitamins, construction, agriculture, geotechnical engineering, marine, taxidermy, and refrigeration manufacturing. Carolina Absorbent Cotton ships its engineered fibers nationwide and globally, while NCFI''s foam products are used in building insulation, roofing systems, and specialty OEM applications across the United States.

Barnhardt emphasizes a legacy of care, stating that it has prioritized the well-being of customers, employees, and suppliers for more than a century. The company highlights its commitment to excellence, fast and reliable delivery, and the sustainable, hypoallergenic properties of its purified cotton as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cotton purification", "Cotton coil manufacturing", "Organic cotton processing", "Reclaimed cotton processing", "Spray foam insulation", "Foam roofing", "Agricultural foam solutions", "Geotechnical foam solutions", "OEM foam insulated panels", "Taxidermy foam solutions", "Marine flotation foam", "Specialty foam solutions"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Vitamin", "Construction", "Agriculture", "Geotechnical", "Marine", "Taxidermy", "Refrigeration", "Consumer goods", "Medical"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Organic cotton", "Reclaimed cotton", "Polyester", "Rayon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1900 -> db, /", "Headquarters Charlotte, NC -> db, /", "Brands: Carolina Absorbent Cotton (75+ years), NCFI (since 1964) -> /", "Products: purified cotton (traditional, organic, reclaimed), cotton/polyester/rayon coils -> /", "Foam solutions: spray foam insulation, foam roofing, agricultural, geotechnical, OEM panels for coolers/refrigeration, taxidermy, marine flotation -> /", "Industries served: pharmaceutical, vitamin, construction, agriculture, geotechnical, marine, taxidermy, refrigeration, consumer/medical -> /", "Differentiators: legacy of care, commitment to excellence, fast reliable delivery, sustainable/hypoallergenic cotton properties -> /", "Company type: manufacturer of cotton and foam products -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''ve been dedicated to delivering the highest-quality purified cotton for over a century.", "founded_year": "1900", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='barnhardt-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bass Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1963 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. The company remains under family leadership, with second-generation president Bill Bass guiding operations after more than 40 years of experience. What began as a specialized industrial camera provider has grown into a U.S.-based manufacturer focused on harsh-environment vision systems.

The company designs and builds ruggedized cameras for extreme conditions: boiler and furnace cameras rated to 4,000 °F, stainless-steel housings for corrosive atmospheres, explosion-proof and flameproof models, and ground-flare camera systems. Its portfolio includes portable furnace cameras for field demonstrations, along with accessories, engineering support, and full-service maintenance. All products are assembled domestically, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Bass Electronics serves industrial process facilities that need reliable visual monitoring in high-temperature, corrosive, explosive, or high-vibration settings. The company emphasizes NDAA-compliant solutions for federal and defense-related projects.

The firm traces its differentiation to over six decades of application-specific development, a two-year warranty on all parts, and a commitment to corrosion protection for electronics exposed to hydrogen sulfide and chlorine. Bass positions its expertise as protecting both people and processes through purpose-built camera systems.', certifications=ARRAY['NDAA Compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial camera design and manufacturing", "Ruggedized camera systems for extreme temperatures", "Explosion-proof/flameproof camera systems", "Corrosion-resistant camera housings (stainless steel)", "High vibration/shock resistant camera systems", "Portable furnace camera systems", "Engineering and design services", "Full service support and maintenance", "NDAA compliance consulting", "Corrosion protection for electronics"], "industries": ["Industrial process facilities", "Process industrial facilities", "Boiler and furnace operations", "Ground flare systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CF Boiler and Furnace Camera 4000\u00b0F/2200\u00b0C", "SE-2012 Stainless Steel Camera", "BE-11 Explosion Proof Camera", "CRC-18 Ground Flare Camera System", "Portable Furnace Camera"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-based manufacturing with over 60 years of experience", "Ruggedized cameras for extreme temperatures up to 4,000 \u00b0F", "Explosion-proof and flameproof certified designs", "NDAA-compliant product line", "Two-year warranty on all parts"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 -> db", "Headquarters Baton Rouge, LA -> db", "Family-owned (second generation) -> /about-us", "Manufactures industrial cameras for extreme environments -> /", "Products: CF Boiler and Furnace Camera, SE-2012, BE-11, CRC-18, Portable Furnace Camera -> /", "Serves industrial process facilities -> /about-us", "NDAA Compliance -> / (blog post)", "Two-year warranty on all parts -> / (product list)", "Corrosion protection for electronics -> / (blog post)", "Second-generation president Bill Bass -> /about-us", "U.S.-based manufacturing -> /", "Ruggedized camera products, accessories, services, engineering, full service support -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Bass Electronics Inc (Bass) is a manufacturing company offering a variety of products and services to help customers view their processes and applications at their industrial processing locations.", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["NDAA Compliance"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bass-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bauer Sheet Metal and Fabricating, Inc. has operated from Scottville, Michigan since 1932. The company began as a sheet metal and steel fabrication shop and has expanded to offer on-site installation services alongside its manufacturing operations.

Today the firm provides precision sheet metal fabrication, structural steel fabrication, and industrial installation. Its manufacturing capabilities include forming, shearing, punching, sawing, flame and plasma cutting, laser cutting, MIG and TIG welding (including food-grade), finishing such as painting, polishing, and powder coating, and secondary machining. The shop runs equipment such as Eagle, Bertsch, and Wysong power rolls, Cincinnati and Wysong shears, a Kamatsu Rason KCR 1251 flame cutter, Hypertherm plasma systems, Bystronic laser cutters, and a Fabriline 60-ton punch. Ultrasonic thickness testing is used for quality verification. The company operates from two locations with an experienced staff, though headcount and annual volume are not disclosed.

Bauer serves the marine and offshore sector under American Bureau of Shipping (ABS) certification, delivering wheelhouse expansions, stack replacements, hull and structural repairs, galley replacements, and custom railings and stairways. For the mining industry, it builds MSHA-compliant equipment including pollution control and dust collection systems, material handling equipment, and structural steel and sheet metal designs. The company also serves food-industry material handling systems, providing custom fabrications such as kitchen hoods, stainless countertops, and flashing, and handles barge repair and general manufacturing repair work.

