UPDATE companies SET description='Broomfield Sheet Metal, Inc. was founded in 1954 in Broomfield, Colorado, and has operated from a 17,000-square-foot facility in Lafayette since 2002. The company is certified as a Minority and Women Business Enterprise (MWBE) and a Disadvantaged Business Enterprise (DBA) by the City and County of Denver. Christine Christensen purchased the business in 2008 and serves as owner and president; the original owner''s philosophy — “Business on a handshake should be good enough” — still guides the operation.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication and HVAC/air-quality-control systems. Capabilities include CNC plasma cutting, TIG and MIG welding, 10-foot shear and brake forming, rolling, sawing, and a range of finishes such as powder coating, anodizing, blackening, patina, and liquid paint. The facility houses a plasma cutting machine, a large will-call area, and extensive material inventory covering aluminum, stainless steel, carbon steel, copper, Corten, galvanized, and structural shapes. The company also designs, fabricates, and installs HVAC equipment for new and existing commercial, industrial, and residential projects.

Customers span homeowners, mill shops, subcontractors, general contractors, restaurant owners, and electrical contractors across the Denver metro area from Colorado Springs to Fort Collins, with the ability to ship nationwide. Recent projects include a beer tap tower for Resolute Brewing Company, a custom steel hood shroud for a residential kitchen, and work featured in the Hensel Phelps Great Hall newsletter.

